#! stone rampart - fieldstone laid without mortar, wide enough at the base to stand on
#! Fills the cell and tiles vertically, the way every shipped wall does.
#! Stone is stipple over solid body, so the face lightens without spending
#! highlight on it. Course tops are broken rather than ruled edge to edge: an
#! unbroken white line every fourth row reads as shelving, and dry-stone courses
#! are not level anyway. Joints are solid body, staggered course to course.
